# Policy-Pilot Core Architecture Rules

## Architectural Boundaries
1. Human-In-The-Loop (HITL): AI outputs are strictly schema-validated recommendations. No LLM action can directly mutate user access entitlements.
2. PII Protection: Mask `employee_id` and `cost_center` across all logger calls, error filters, and telemetry pipelines.
3. Deterministic Integrity: Use Zod or class-validator on all inputs and outputs. Never accept unvalidated JSON from external webhooks or LLM outputs.

## Code Quality Standards
- Strict TypeScript: No `any` types allowed under any circumstances.
- Explicit Error Handling: Never swallow errors. Wrap caught exceptions in NestJS Exception Filters or return explicit error results.
- No Placeholders: Never generate code with ellipses (`// ... rest unchanged`) or stubbed function bodies.
